OL,3,GNEWSAHopes for needle-free allergy
OL,4,Aspray to be approved
OL,5,
OL,6,FMedics have said an adrenaline nasal
OL,7,Fspray to treat allergic reactions
OL,8,F"could be a real step forward" if
OL,9,Fapproved in Guernsey.
OL,11,FEURneffy is a needle-free medicine used
OL,12,Fto treat of severe allergic reactions,
OL,13,Fknown as anaphylaxis, which specialists
OL,14,Fsaid could help those with a fear of
OL,15,Finjections.
OL,17,FThe spray was approved by the UK
OL,18,Fmedicines regulator in July 2025 but it
OL,19,Fis not currently available on
OL,20,FGuernsey's prescribing list.
OL,23,APub: 10-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
